Do not rely only on disabling a frontend button.

Before confirming a booking, validate:

- The worker exists.
- The worker is verified.
- The worker is active and eligible.
- The worker has the requested skill.
- The worker serves the requested station.
- The worker is available for the requested time.
- The worker has no conflicting active booking.
- The passenger is authorized to create the booking.
- The complaint, if supplied, belongs to the passenger.
- The service category is valid.

If two requests attempt to reserve the same worker simultaneously, the backend must safely accept only compatible bookings.

Return a clear error when the selected worker is no longer available.

The passenger should be able to select another eligible worker.

Avoid duplicate booking creation when a user double-clicks the booking button or retries a request after a network delay.

Use idempotency keys or an equivalent safe mechanism if supported by the existing architecture.

